  "contract": {
    "configSchema": {
      "type": "object",
      "properties": {
        "laneRequestPath": {
          "type": "string",
          "pattern": "^/"
        },
        "tiltGravityPath": {
          "type": "string",
          "pattern": "^/"
        },
        "aimPath": {
          "type": "string",
          "pattern": "^/",
          "description": "aimPath is a JSON pointer into global state (no /state prefix) whose value is a two-number direction vector [dx,dy], not an absolute target position. Both components must be finite with absolute value<=32000. By default the Runtime divides by abs(dx)+abs(dy) (L1 normalization); aimMetric=euclidean selects circular geometry. [0,0] falls back to fireDirection, default right. Positive x is right and positive y is up. An aimPath overrides autoTarget; without aimPath, autoTarget=true may aim at the selected live target, otherwise fireDirection is used. Projectile and hitscan fire consume this direction. A rule state.set effect commits after physics, so changing aim and firing in the same Tick uses the previously committed aim; the new aim is visible to the next Tick."
        },
        "aimMetric": {
          "enum": [
            "manhattan",
            "euclidean"
          ],
          "description": "Optional, defaults to manhattan for compatibility. euclidean normalizes aim by L2 length, uses squared center distance for target admission and ordering, and uses the same radius for the hitscan ray. A supplied Euclidean weaponRange must be an integer from 1 to 32000. Projectile components are rounded symmetrically to the nearest integer (half away from zero), so integer velocities approximate rather than exactly preserve continuous speed."
        },
